    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass. `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nRedesigned owner identity so the `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>` and everything derived from it follows the new region-and-hash identity.\n\n**New shared helper** \u2014 `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/CustomerCodes.java`\n- `build(owner)` \u2192 `region(owner) + \"-\" + hash8` where `hash8` is the first 8 upper-case hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`.\n- `region(owner)` \u2192 region from postcode range (NSW/VIC/QLD), falling back to the city table, then `\"UNKNOWN\"`.\n- `regionOf(customerCode)` \u2192 the REGION segment (before the first `-`) for reading locality back off the identity.\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode`** \u2014 dropped the per-city sequence and the `OwnerRepository` dependency; now just `owner.setCustomerCode(CustomerCodes.build(owner))`. All fields it needs (normalized telephone, last name, postcode/city) are already set by `BuildOwner` earlier in the pipeline.\n\n**`OwnerMapper`**\n- `locality(owner)` now derives from the identity \u2014 the REGION segment of `customerCode` \u2014 falling back to a direct region computation only for legacy seed owners that have no `customerCode`. Removed the now-duplicated `CITY_REGION`/`REGION_POSTCODES`/`regionFromPostcode` (single source of truth is `CustomerCodes`).\n- `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` already read from `customerCode`, so they automatically reflect the new identity; only the doc example was updated (`NSW-1A2B3C4D-M26`).\n\n**Audit** \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated` already logs `owner.getCustomerCode()`, so it now records the new identity (verified in the run: `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`).\n\nNo schema change needed \u2014 `customer_code VARCHAR(20)` comfortably holds the new max of 16 chars (`UNKNOWN-` + 8 hex).\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash` and the full suite are green.",
